{"title":"2010 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 12A Problems\">2010 AMC 12A #9</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems\">2010 AMC 10A #17</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_the_Beauty_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by the Beauty of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A solid cube has side length 3 inches. A 2-inch by 2-inch square hole is cut into the center of each face. The edges of each cut are parallel to the edges of the cube, and each hole goes all the way through the cube. What is the volume, in cubic inches, of the remaining solid?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/3/443e77961d5932cb9ef01b8d911a5ccb55ca9a59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 7 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 8 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 10 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 12 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"376\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Imagine making the cuts one at a time. The first cut removes a box <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e00c42619c12f749a3bb75e5b4afcadc7bafd32c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\times 2\\times 3$\" width=\"71\" height=\"12\" />. The second cut removes two boxes, each of dimensions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc5de5cb27afbd247a2fcd9e841b4c6874180f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\times 2\\times 0.5$\" width=\"85\" height=\"12\" />, and the third cut does the same as the second cut, on the last two faces. Hence the total volume of all cuts is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/f/59f7389c3fbb2e4636e89c605442703d4da62426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 + 4 + 4 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore the volume of the rest of the cube is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c82eb5dcf2782cbd0fa6df391f9ef104645f4645.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^3 - 20 = 27 - 20 = \\boxed{7\\ \\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"219\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We can visualize it has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cube with a hollow <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> center, along with 6 \"windows\" cut out too. The cube formula gives the volume of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cube as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a4cab0e2e4cb14f95a8217edd2ed7d48e0aa8f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^3 = 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/6/ee6f6eec064e49c853dedcd15531994cbec23c24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3 = 8.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" /> Additionally, the area of the \"windows\" is the 2x2 cut along with a thickness of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/7/6d7039f6938b050e2509cb2d51def48b7cc00794.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(3-2)}{2} = \\frac{1}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"40\" /> The volume of all 6 windows is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/0/09097059557447cfb7a1789c9f825e0860ed5857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6(\\frac{1}{2})(2)(2) = 12.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"132\" height=\"38\" /> This gives us our answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/0/9102f49f21c7a00639ed5e4768d8e4ec83a2f5c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27 - 8 - 12 = \\boxed{7\\ \\textbf{(A)}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"176\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We can use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Principle_of_Inclusion-Exclusion\" title=\"Principle of Inclusion-Exclusion\">Principle of Inclusion-Exclusion</a> (PIE) to find the final volume of the cube.\n</p><p>There are 3 \"cuts\" through the cube that go from one end to the other. Each of these \"cuts\" has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/8/ae8fdb2e885ba6e56da28228574598968b7ba0d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 2 \\times 3=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" /> cubic inches. However, we can not just sum their volumes, as\nthe central <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/c/e1c22f5c1912027b16c00cd431cb20cda62ed955.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\times 2\\times 2$\" width=\"71\" height=\"12\" /> cube is included in each of these three cuts. To get the correct result, we can take the sum of the volumes of the three cuts, and subtract the volume of the central cube twice.\n</p><p>Hence the total volume of the cuts is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66c15a2ac38e6ee451895551e7eb72dba099b6db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(2 \\times 2 \\times 3) - 2(2\\times 2\\times 2) = 36 - 16 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"336\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore the volume of the rest of the cube is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c82eb5dcf2782cbd0fa6df391f9ef104645f4645.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^3 - 20 = 27 - 20 = \\boxed{7\\ \\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"219\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We can visualize the final figure and see a cubic frame. We can find the volume of the figure by adding up the volumes of the edges and corners.\n</p><p>Each edge can be seen as a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/96189382193e5a3430aadd81400e0df04b65b5f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\times 0.5\\times 0.5$\" width=\"99\" height=\"12\" /> box, and each corner can be seen as a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b7c89aee001e4b69ec09f207b4bb598fbe50c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.5\\times 0.5\\times 0.5$\" width=\"113\" height=\"12\" /> box.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/6/f462a7033eeb1a206f1926296f223a8c5d150e29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12\\cdot{\\frac{1}{2}} + 8\\cdot{\\frac{1}{8}} = 6+1 = \\boxed{7\\ \\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"246\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_the_Beauty_of_Math\">Video Solution by the Beauty of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by the Beauty of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rsURe5Xh-j0?t=354\">https://youtu.be/rsURe5Xh-j0?t=354</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A\">2010 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b